          <Data name="Description_EN">
            <value><![CDATA[Hadrian's Baths are among the largest Roman bath complexes in Leptis Magna. Built during the reign of Emperor Hadrian in the 2nd century AD, the complex served as a major social and recreational center, featuring hot, warm, and cold bathing halls, courtyards, and richly decorated architectural elements.‏‏‏]]></value>
